      "value": "Extra information.\nI was on the world where my friend is. First time shutter started after short time smooth movement. When i saw someone in stream touched me much earlier than what i see myself, i did rejoin same world try to re-sync with my friends. But shutter is already seen after very short time.\nRejoined again same world, shutter started almost immediately.\n\nI give up and went to another world. There it went okay for a while, and then i saw shutter effect after approx 15 minutes. That is 4 times in short time, and both worlds are not even maxed out.\n\nThe extra note is i am in VRChat for more than 6 hours. When you're playing for long time in VRChat, the chance for shuttering seems raised more and more. So it's getting worser.\n\nIf you just started VRChat, there is no shutter and everyone moves smooth around. The chance for shutter raise a bit by time you played in VRChat. It's like something in VRChat networking is getting \"full\", like buffer is full and then network system broke and bugged more. This effect will raise more if you played more than 6 hours.\n\nPretty much players are for long time in VRChat (especially streamers) so this is just not great to see the shutter effect.\n\nThat is what i think.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
